§ `2018, c. 12, s. 406 -- remediation agreements for an offence alleged before section 404 came into force`

-- 406 (1) A remediation agreement may be entered into in respect of an offence alleged to have been committed before the day on which section 404 comes into force.
-- A permission with no named actor (the parties to a remediation agreement are in section 715.3, part ccc25): encoded as a decision only; no actor is invented.
-- src:19177 | Offence allegedly committed before section 404 comes into force
-- src:19178 | 406 (1) A remediation agreement may be entered into in respect of an offence alleged to have been committed before the day on which section 404 comes into force.
@ref 2018, c. 12, s. 406(1) (src:19177-19178)
GIVEN `the day on which section 404 of 2018, c. 12 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the offence is alleged to have been committed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2018 c 12 s 406(1) a remediation agreement may be entered into in respect of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the day the offence is alleged to have been committed` LESS THAN `the day on which section 404 of 2018, c. 12 comes into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of an offence alleged to have been committed before the day on which section 404 comes into force"

-- (2) For the purpose of subsection (1), remediation agreement and offence have the same meaning as in section 715.3 as enacted by section 404.
-- The meaning is in section 715.3 (another part): its answer is an input, carried through.
-- src:19179 | Meaning
-- src:19180 | (2) For the purpose of subsection (1), remediation agreement and offence have the same meaning as in section 715.3 of the Criminal Code, as enacted by section 404.
@ref 2018, c. 12, s. 406(2) (src:19179-19180)
DECLARE `2018 c 12 s 406(2) term` IS ONE OF
    `2018 c 12 s 406(2) remediation agreement`
    `2018 c 12 s 406(2) offence`
    `2018 c 12 s 406(2) another term`

@ref 2018, c. 12, s. 406(2) (src:19179-19180)
GIVEN term IS A `2018 c 12 s 406(2) term`
      `s 715.3 the thing is within the meaning that remediation agreement or offence has` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2018 c 12 s 406(2) the term has the meaning it has in section 715.3` MEANS
    CONSIDER term
    WHEN `2018 c 12 s 406(2) remediation agreement` THEN `s 715.3 the thing is within the meaning that remediation agreement or offence has`
    WHEN `2018 c 12 s 406(2) offence` THEN `s 715.3 the thing is within the meaning that remediation agreement or offence has`
    WHEN `2018 c 12 s 406(2) another term` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of subsection (1), remediation agreement and offence have the same meaning"

§ `2018, c. 21, ss. 10 and 32 to 38 -- impaired driving: instruments, appeals, technicians`

-- 10 Any approved instrument, approved screening device or approved container approved under 254(1) as it read immediately before the day subsection 3(1) comes into force is deemed to be approved, respectively, under 254.01.
-- src:19183 | Approved instrument, approved screening device, approved container
-- src:19184 | 10 Any approved instrument, approved screening device or approved container approved under subsection 254(1) of the Criminal Code, as it read immediately before the day on which subsection 3(1) of this Act comes into force, is deemed to be approved as an approved instrument, approved screening device or approved container, respectively, under section 254.01 of the Criminal Code as enacted by section 4 of this Act.
@ref 2018, c. 21, s. 10 (src:19183-19184)
DECLARE `2018 c 21 s 10 kind of thing approved` IS ONE OF
    `2018 c 21 s 10 an approved instrument`
    `2018 c 21 s 10 an approved screening device`
    `2018 c 21 s 10 an approved container`
    `2018 c 21 s 10 something else`

@ref 2018, c. 21, s. 10 (src:19183-19184)
