`2018 c 21 s 34(1) an appeal may be taken against the order` MEANS
    IF `the order was made under section 259 as that section read from time to time before that day`
       AND `the day the appeal is taken` AT LEAST `the day on which section 21 of 2018, c. 21 comes into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appeal may be taken on or after the day on which section 21 of this Act comes into force against an order made under section 259"

