§ `2018, c. 29, s. 74 -- hearing under subsection 278.3(5): sixty days`

-- 2018 c 29 s 74: a continuing application for a hearing on the day itself or within 60 days after it. Inside the period JUST TRUE; outside it the text's own period says no (JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)); a hearing the subsection does not refer to is outside the grant (NOTHING).
-- src:19225 | Hearing — subsection 278.3(5)
-- src:19226 | 74 Subsection 278.3(5) of the Criminal Code, as that subsection read immediately before the day on which section 24 comes into force, continues to apply in respect of any hearing referred to in that subsection that takes place on that day or within 60 days after that day.
@ref 2018, c. 29, s. 74 (src:19225-19226)
GIVEN `the day on which section 24 of 2018, c. 29 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the hearing takes place` IS A DATE
      `the hearing is a hearing referred to in subsection 278.3(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2018 c 29 s 74 subsection 278.3(5) as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the hearing is a hearing referred to in subsection 278.3(5)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any hearing referred to in that subsection"
        IF `the day the hearing takes place` AT LEAST `the day on which section 24 of 2018, c. 29 comes into force` AND `the day the hearing takes place` AT MOST (`the day on which section 24 of 2018, c. 29 comes into force` PLUS 60) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "takes place on that day or within 60 days after that day"


