§ `2019, c. 25, ss. 354 to 360 -- bail and procedure: documents deemed, re-election, the limitation period`

-- 354 A person bound by a promise to appear given under the Code before the day subsection 1(3) comes into force is deemed, on and after that day, to be bound by an appearance notice as defined in section 2.
-- "on and after that day": the period is fixed in the text's own words, so before that day the text says no (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)); a person not bound by such a promise is outside the wording.
-- src:19245 | Promise to appear
-- src:19246 | 354 A person who is bound by a promise to appear given under the Criminal Code before the day on which subsection 1(3) of this Act comes into force is deemed, on and after that day, to be bound by an appearance notice as defined in section 2 of the Criminal Code, as amended by subsection 1(3) of this Act.
@ref 2019, c. 25, s. 354 (src:19245-19246)
GIVEN `the day on which subsection 1(3) of 2019, c. 25 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the question is about` IS A DATE
      `the person is bound by a promise to appear given under the Criminal Code before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2019 c 25 s 354 the person is deemed to be bound by an appearance notice as defined in section 2` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is bound by a promise to appear given under the Criminal Code before that day` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is bound by a promise to appear given under the Criminal Code before the day on which subsection 1(3) of this Act comes into force"
        IF `the day the question is about` LESS THAN `the day on which subsection 1(3) of 2019, c. 25 comes into force` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed, on and after that day"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 355 A person bound by an undertaking given under section 499 or subsection 503(2.1) before that day is deemed, on and after that day, to be bound by an undertaking as defined in section 2.
-- src:19249 | Undertaking given to peace officer or officer in charge
-- src:19250 | 355 A person who is bound by an undertaking given under section 499 or subsection 503(2.1) of the Criminal Code before the day on which subsection 1(3) of this Act comes into force is deemed, on and after that day, to be bound by an undertaking as defined in section 2 of the Criminal Code, as amended by subsection 1(3) of this Act.
@ref 2019, c. 25, s. 355 (src:19249-19250)
GIVEN `the day on which subsection 1(3) of 2019, c. 25 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the question is about` IS A DATE
      `the provision the undertaking was given under` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person is bound by an undertaking given before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2019 c 25 s 355 the person is deemed to be bound by an undertaking as defined in section 2` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is bound by an undertaking given before that day` AND `the provision is section 499 or subsection 503(2.1)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is bound by an undertaking given under section 499 or subsection 503(2.1) of the Criminal Code before the day"
        IF `the day the question is about` LESS THAN `the day on which subsection 1(3) of 2019, c. 25 comes into force` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed, on and after that day"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the provision is section 499 or subsection 503(2.1)` MEANS
                `the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `section` EQUALS 499
            OR  (`the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `section` EQUALS 503 AND `the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2.1)")

-- 356 A person bound by a recognizance entered into under section 498 or 499 or subsection 503(2) before that day is deemed, on and after that day, to be bound by an UNDERTAKING as defined in section 2.
-- src:19253 | Recognizance entered into before peace officer or officer in charge
-- src:19254 | 356 A person who is bound by a recognizance entered into under section 498 or 499 or subsection 503(2) of the Criminal Code before the day on which subsection 1(3) of this Act comes into force is deemed, on and after that day, to be bound by an undertaking as defined in section 2 of the Criminal Code, as amended by subsection 1(3) of this Act.
@ref 2019, c. 25, s. 356 (src:19253-19254)
GIVEN `the day on which subsection 1(3) of 2019, c. 25 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the question is about` IS A DATE
      `the provision the recognizance was entered into under` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person is bound by a recognizance entered into before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2019 c 25 s 356 the person is deemed to be bound by an undertaking as defined in section 2` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is bound by a recognizance entered into before that day` AND `the provision is section 498 or 499 or subsection 503(2)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is bound by a recognizance entered into under section 498 or 499 or subsection 503(2) of the Criminal Code before the day"
        IF `the day the question is about` LESS THAN `the day on which subsection 1(3) of 2019, c. 25 comes into force` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed, on and after that day"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the provision is section 498 or 499 or subsection 503(2)` MEANS
                `the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `section` EQUALS 498
            OR  `the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `section` EQUALS 499
            OR  (`the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `section` EQUALS 503 AND `the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)")

-- 357 A person bound by an undertaking given under subsection 503(3.1) or section 515, 522, 524, 525, 597, 679, 683, 816 or 832 before that day is deemed, on and after that day, to be bound by a RELEASE ORDER as defined in section 2.
-- src:19257 | Undertaking given to judge or justice
-- src:19258 | 357 A person who is bound by an undertaking given under subsection 503(3.1) or section 515, 522, 524, 525, 597, 679, 683, 816 or 832 of the Criminal Code before the day on which subsection 1(3) of this Act comes into force is deemed, on and after that day, to be bound by a release order as defined in section 2 of the Criminal Code, as amended by subsection 1(3) of this Act.
@ref 2019, c. 25, s. 357 (src:19257-19258)
GIVEN `the day on which subsection 1(3) of 2019, c. 25 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the question is about` IS A DATE
      `the provision the undertaking was given under` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person is bound by an undertaking given before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2019 c 25 s 357 the person is deemed to be bound by a release order as defined in section 2` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is bound by an undertaking given before that day` AND `the provision is subsection 503(3.1) or section 515, 522, 524, 525, 597, 679, 683, 816 or 832`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is bound by an undertaking given under subsection 503(3.1) or section 515, 522, 524, 525, 597, 679, 683, 816 or 832 of the Criminal Code before the day"
        IF `the day the question is about` LESS THAN `the day on which subsection 1(3) of 2019, c. 25 comes into force` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed, on and after that day"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the provision is subsection 503(3.1) or section 515, 522, 524, 525, 597, 679, 683, 816 or 832` MEANS
                (`the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `section` EQUALS 503 AND `the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(3.1)")
            OR  `the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `section` EQUALS 515 OR `the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `section` EQUALS 522
            OR  `the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `section` EQUALS 524 OR `the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `section` EQUALS 525
            OR  `the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `section` EQUALS 597 OR `the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `section` EQUALS 679
            OR  `the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `section` EQUALS 683 OR `the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `section` EQUALS 816
            OR  `the provision the undertaking was given under`'s `section` EQUALS 832

-- 358 A person bound by a recognizance entered into under subsection 503(3.1) or section 515, 522, 524, 525, 679, 683, 816 or 832 before that day is deemed, on and after that day, to be bound by a RELEASE ORDER as defined in section 2. (No 597 in this list.)
-- src:19261 | Recognizance entered into before judge or justice
-- src:19262 | 358 A person who is bound by a recognizance entered into under subsection 503(3.1) or section 515, 522, 524, 525, 679, 683, 816 or 832 of the Criminal Code before the day on which subsection 1(3) of this Act comes into force is deemed, on and after that day, to be bound by a release order as defined in section 2 of the Criminal Code, as amended by subsection 1(3) of this Act.
@ref 2019, c. 25, s. 358 (src:19261-19262)
GIVEN `the day on which subsection 1(3) of 2019, c. 25 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the question is about` IS A DATE
      `the provision the recognizance was entered into under` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person is bound by a recognizance entered into before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2019 c 25 s 358 the person is deemed to be bound by a release order as defined in section 2` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is bound by a recognizance entered into before that day` AND `the provision is subsection 503(3.1) or section 515, 522, 524, 525, 679, 683, 816 or 832`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is bound by a recognizance entered into under subsection 503(3.1) or section 515, 522, 524, 525, 679, 683, 816 or 832 of the Criminal Code before the day"
        IF `the day the question is about` LESS THAN `the day on which subsection 1(3) of 2019, c. 25 comes into force` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed, on and after that day"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the provision is subsection 503(3.1) or section 515, 522, 524, 525, 679, 683, 816 or 832` MEANS
                (`the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `section` EQUALS 503 AND `the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(3.1)")
            OR  `the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `section` EQUALS 515 OR `the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `section` EQUALS 522
            OR  `the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `section` EQUALS 524 OR `the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `section` EQUALS 525
            OR  `the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `section` EQUALS 679 OR `the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `section` EQUALS 683
            OR  `the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `section` EQUALS 816 OR `the provision the recognizance was entered into under`'s `section` EQUALS 832

-- 359 Any person accused of an offence before the day section 254 comes into force, and who is in one of the cases described in 561(1)(b)(i) or 561(2) or 561.1(2), may, if they have not already done so and despite those provisions,
-- elect another mode of trial not later than 14 days before the day first appointed for the trial, and may do so after that time with the written consent of the prosecutor.
-- src:19265 | Right to re-elect
-- src:19266 | 359 Any person accused of an offence before the day on which section 254 of this Act comes into force and who finds themselves in one of the cases described in subparagraph 561(1)(b)(i) or subsection 561(2) or 561.1(2) of the Criminal Code, as enacted by this Act, may, if they have not already done so and despite those provisions, elect another mode of trial not later than 14 days before the day first appointed for the trial and they may do so after that time with the written consent of the prosecutor.
@ref 2019, c. 25, s. 359 (src:19265-19266)
GIVEN `the person was accused of the offence before the day on which section 254 of 2019, c. 25 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 561 the person is in one of the cases described in subparagraph 561(1)(b)(i) or subsection 561(2) or 561.1(2) as enacted by 2019, c. 25` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has already elected another mode of trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person elects another mode of trial` IS A DATE
      `the day first appointed for the trial` IS A DATE
      `the prosecutor consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- Named for a power (a person may elect): a failed "if they have not already done so" is the text's limit on the grant, so NOTHING (the other reading, the text's no, is fork F25 in NOTES.md); the 14-day deadline below keeps JUST FALSE (a period fixed in the text's own words, listed in the fork register).
`2019 c 25 s 359 the person may elect another mode of trial` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person was accused of the offence before the day on which section 254 of 2019, c. 25 comes into force` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person accused of an offence before the day on which section 254 of this Act comes into force"
        IF NOT (`s 561 the person is in one of the cases described in subparagraph 561(1)(b)(i) or subsection 561(2) or 561.1(2) as enacted by 2019, c. 25` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in one of the cases described in section 561 is for part ccc21 and is not answered JUST TRUE
        IF `the person has already elected another mode of trial` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if they have not already done so"
        IF `the day the person elects another mode of trial` AT MOST (`the day first appointed for the trial` MINUS 14) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the prosecutor consents in writing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than 14 days before the day first appointed for the trial"

-- 360 For any offence punishable on summary conviction committed before the coming into force of section 315, no proceedings shall be instituted more than six months after the time when the subject matter of the proceedings arose,
-- unless the prosecutor and the defendant so agree. The name says only what the section decides: the proceedings are within (or, by agreement, released from) the six-month limit; a case outside the section's scope is NOTHING.
-- src:19269 | Limitation period for summary offences
-- src:19270 | 360 For any offence punishable on summary conviction committed before the coming into force of section 315, no proceedings shall be instituted more than six months after the time when the subject matter of the proceedings arose, unless the prosecutor and the defendant so agree.
@ref 2019, c. 25, s. 360 (src:19269-19270)
GIVEN `the offence is punishable on summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the offence was committed` IS A DATE
      `the day on which section 315 of 2019, c. 25 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the subject matter of the proceedings arose` IS A DATE
      `the day the proceedings are instituted` IS A DATE
      `the prosecutor and the defendant so agree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2019 c 25 s 360 the proceedings are within the time limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the offence is punishable on summary conviction` AND `the day the offence was committed` LESS THAN `the day on which section 315 of 2019, c. 25 comes into force`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For any offence punishable on summary conviction committed before the coming into force of section 315"
        IF `the prosecutor and the defendant so agree` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the day the proceedings are instituted` AT MOST (`add months` `the day the subject matter of the proceedings arose` 6) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no proceedings shall be instituted more than six months after the time when the subject matter of the proceedings arose"

§ `2021, c. 2, s. 4 -- medical assistance in dying: a request made before royal assent`

-- 4 A medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provides MAID to a person who, before the day the Act received royal assent, had signed and dated a written request must provide it in accordance with section 241.2 as it read
-- immediately before that day, other than paragraph 241.2(3)(g), and with subsections 241.2(3.2) to (3.5) as enacted by this Act. The core has no party for a medical practitioner: this module declares its own (NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- src:19281 | Request made prior to assent
-- src:19282 | 4 A medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provides medical assistance in dying to a person who, before the day on which this Act receives royal assent, had signed and dated a written request for medical assistance in dying must provide it in accordance with section 241.2 of the Criminal Code as it read immediately before that day, other than paragraph 241.2(3)(g), and with subsections 241.2(3.2) to (3.5) of that Act, as enacted by this Act.
@ref 2021, c. 2, s. 4 (src:19281-19282)
DECLARE `2021 c 2 s 4 party` IS ONE OF
    `2021 c 2 s 4 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner`

DECLARE `2021 c 2 s 4 act` IS ONE OF
    `2021 c 2 s 4 provide medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2 as it read immediately before that day, other than paragraph 241.2(3)(g), and with subsections 241.2(3.2) to (3.5) as enacted by that Act`

@ref 2021, c. 2, s. 4 (src:19281-19282)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `2021 c 2 s 4 party` `2021 c 2 s 4 act`
`2021 c 2 s 4 the provider must provide medical assistance in dying in accordance with the old section 241.2` MEANS
    PARTY `2021 c 2 s 4 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner`
    MUST `2021 c 2 s 4 provide medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2 as it read immediately before that day, other than paragraph 241.2(3)(g), and with subsections 241.2(3.2) to (3.5) as enacted by that Act`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `2021 c 2 s 4 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner` BECAUSE "medical assistance in dying was provided to a person who had signed and dated a written request before the day on which 2021, c. 2 received royal assent otherwise than in accordance with section 241.2 as it read immediately before that day"

@ref 2021, c. 2, s. 4 (src:19281-19282)
GIVEN `the provider is a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person signed and dated the written request for medical assistance in dying` IS A DATE
      `the day on which 2021, c. 2 received royal assent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2021 c 2 s 4 the provider must provide it in accordance with the old section 241.2 and subsections 241.2(3.2) to (3.5)` MEANS
    IF `the provider is a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner`
       AND `the day the person signed and dated the written request for medical assistance in dying` LESS THAN `the day on which 2021, c. 2 received royal assent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provides medical assistance in dying to a person who, before the day on which this Act receives royal assent, had signed and dated a written request"

§ `2022, c. 17, ss. 76 to 78 -- the amendments apply to ongoing proceedings, but the old law continues for some authorizations, warrants and seizures`

-- 77 (1) The Criminal Code, as it read immediately before the day this Act comes into force, continues to apply with respect to (a) an authorization given under 184.3 before that day; (b) a warrant issued under 487.1 before that day;
-- (c) any other warrant issued before that day to which 487.1, as it read immediately before that day, applied; (d) an application for an authorization or warrant in (a) to (c) submitted, and not decided, before that day; and
-- (e) any authorization given or warrant issued on or after that day on the basis of an application in (d).
-- src:19307 | Continuation — authorizations and warrants
-- src:19308 | 77 (1) The Criminal Code, as it read immediately before the day on which this Act comes into force, continues to apply with respect to
-- src:19309 | (a) an authorization given under section 184.3 of the Criminal Code before that day;
-- src:19310 | (b) a warrant issued under section 487.1 of that Act before that day;
-- src:19311 | (c) any other warrant issued before that day to which that section 487.1, as it read immediately before that day, applied;
-- src:19312 | (d) an application for an authorization or warrant referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (c) that is submitted, and in respect of which no decision has been made, before that day; and
-- src:19313 | (e) any authorization that is given or warrant that is issued on or after that day on the basis of an application referred to in paragraph (d).
@ref 2022, c. 17, s. 77(1) (src:19307-19313)
DECLARE `2022 c 17 s 77(1) kind of thing` IS ONE OF
    `2022 c 17 s 77(1) an authorization given under section 184.3`   -- (a)
    `2022 c 17 s 77(1) a warrant issued under section 487.1`   -- (b)
    `2022 c 17 s 77(1) any other warrant to which section 487.1, as it read immediately before that day, applied`   -- (c)
    `2022 c 17 s 77(1) an application for an authorization or warrant referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (c), submitted and not decided`   -- (d)
    `2022 c 17 s 77(1) an authorization given or a warrant issued on the basis of an application referred to in paragraph (d)`   -- (e)
    `2022 c 17 s 77(1) something else`

@ref 2022, c. 17, s. 77(1) (src:19307-19313)
GIVEN `the day on which 2022, c. 17 comes into force` IS A DATE
      kind IS A `2022 c 17 s 77(1) kind of thing`
      `the day it was given, issued or submitted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2022 c 17 s 77(1) the Criminal Code as it read immediately before that day continues to apply` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `2022 c 17 s 77(1) an authorization given under section 184.3` THEN `before the day`
    WHEN `2022 c 17 s 77(1) a warrant issued under section 487.1` THEN `before the day`
    WHEN `2022 c 17 s 77(1) any other warrant to which section 487.1, as it read immediately before that day, applied` THEN `before the day`
    WHEN `2022 c 17 s 77(1) an application for an authorization or warrant referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (c), submitted and not decided` THEN `before the day`
    WHEN `2022 c 17 s 77(1) an authorization given or a warrant issued on the basis of an application referred to in paragraph (d)` THEN
        IF `the day it was given, issued or submitted` AT LEAST `the day on which 2022, c. 17 comes into force`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any authorization that is given or warrant that is issued on or after that day on the basis of an application referred to in paragraph (d)"
    WHEN `2022 c 17 s 77(1) something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "continues to apply with respect to" names the things it covers and does not say it covers nothing else
    WHERE
        `before the day` MEANS
            IF `the day it was given, issued or submitted` LESS THAN `the day on which 2022, c. 17 comes into force`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before that day"

-- 78 Section 489.1, as it read immediately before the day this Act comes into force, continues to apply with respect to anything seized under a warrant issued under the Criminal Code or another Act of Parliament if the application for the warrant was made before that day.
-- src:19316 | Continuation — section 489.1 of Criminal Code
-- src:19317 | 78 Section 489.1 of the Criminal Code, as that section read immediately before the day on which this Act comes into force, continues to apply with respect to anything seized under a warrant issued under the Criminal Code or another Act of Parliament if the application for the warrant was made before that day.
@ref 2022, c. 17, s. 78 (src:19316-19317)
GIVEN `the day on which 2022, c. 17 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the thing was seized under a warrant issued under the Criminal Code or another Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application for the warrant was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2022 c 17 s 78 section 489.1 as it read immediately before that day continues to apply to the thing seized` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the thing was seized under a warrant issued under the Criminal Code or another Act of Parliament` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with respect to anything seized under a warrant issued under the Criminal Code or another Act of Parliament"
        IF `the day the application for the warrant was made` LESS THAN `the day on which 2022, c. 17 comes into force` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the application for the warrant was made before that day"

-- 76 For greater certainty, but subject to sections 77 and 78, the amendments made by this Act also apply with respect to proceedings that are ongoing on the day this Act comes into force.
-- A composition: sections 77 and 78 govern first, so where either says the old law continues the amendments do not apply; where either is not covered the answer is not covered.
-- src:19303 | Clarification — immediate application
-- src:19304 | 76 For greater certainty, but subject to sections 77 and 78, the amendments made by this Act also apply with respect to proceedings that are ongoing on the day on which this Act comes into force.
@ref 2022, c. 17, s. 76 (src:19303-19304)
GIVEN `the proceedings are ongoing on the day on which 2022, c. 17 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of section 77 for the matter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of section 78 for the matter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2022 c 17 s 76 the amendments made by 2022, c. 17 apply to the proceedings, subject to sections 77 and 78` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are ongoing on the day on which 2022, c. 17 comes into force` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with respect to proceedings that are ongoing on the day on which this Act comes into force"
        IF `the answer of section 77 for the matter` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of section 78 for the matter` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but subject to sections 77 and 78"
        IF `the answer of section 77 for the matter` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the answer of section 78 for the matter` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether sections 77 and 78 take the matter out of the amendments is for those sections' answers
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `2023, c. 26, ss. 613 to 615 -- the criminal rate of interest and payday loans`

-- 613 The words and expressions used in sections 614 and 615 have the same meaning as in sections 347 and 347.1. A pointer: the meaning is in sections 347 and 347.1 (another part), taken as an input.
-- src:19335 | Words and expressions
-- src:19336 | 613 The words and expressions used in sections 614 and 615 have the same meaning as in sections 347 and 347.1 of the Criminal Code.
@ref 2023, c. 26, s. 613 (src:19335-19336)
GIVEN `the word or expression is used in section 614 or 615 of 2023, c. 26` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 347 the word or expression is within the meaning it has in sections 347 and 347.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2023 c 26 s 613 the word or expression has the meaning it has in sections 347 and 347.1` MEANS
    IF `the word or expression is used in section 614 or 615 of 2023, c. 26`
    THEN `s 347 the word or expression is within the meaning it has in sections 347 and 347.1`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The words and expressions used in sections 614 and 615"

-- 614 For the purposes of 347(1), the definition criminal rate in 347(2), as it reads on the day 610(1) comes into force, does not apply to a receipt of interest that, on or after that day, is at a criminal rate, if the payment arises from an agreement
-- entered into before that day and the interest would not have been at a criminal rate under 347(2) as it read before that day. A flat negative under its own conditions; outside them the section is silent (NOTHING).
-- src:19339 | Subsection 347(1) of Criminal Code
-- src:19340 | 614 For the purposes of subsection 347(1) of the Criminal Code, the definition criminal rate in subsection 347(2) of that Act, as it reads on the day on which subsection 610(1) comes into force, does not apply in respect of any receipt of a payment or partial payment of interest that, on or after that day, is interest at a criminal rate, if the payment arises from an agreement or arrangement to receive interest that was entered into before that day and the interest that arises from that agreement or arrangement would not have been at a criminal rate, as defined in subsection 347(2) of the Criminal Code, as that subsection 347(2) read before that day.
@ref 2023, c. 26, s. 614 (src:19339-19340)
GIVEN `the day on which subsection 610(1) of 2023, c. 26 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the payment or partial payment of interest is received` IS A DATE
      `the day the agreement or arrangement to receive interest was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the interest that arises from that agreement would not have been at a criminal rate, as defined in subsection 347(2) as it read before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2023 c 26 s 614 the definition criminal rate in subsection 347(2), as it reads on that day, applies to the receipt` MEANS
    IF `the day the payment or partial payment of interest is received` AT LEAST `the day on which subsection 610(1) of 2023, c. 26 comes into force`
       AND `the day the agreement or arrangement to receive interest was entered into` LESS THAN `the day on which subsection 610(1) of 2023, c. 26 comes into force`
       AND `the interest that arises from that agreement would not have been at a criminal rate, as defined in subsection 347(2) as it read before that day`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply in respect of any receipt of a payment or partial payment of interest"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the payment arises from an agreement or arrangement to receive interest that was entered into before that day"

-- 615 Paragraph 347.1(2)(a.1), as it reads on the day subsection 612(1) comes into force, does not apply to a person who (a) entered into a payday loan agreement to receive interest before that day; or
-- (b) on or after that day, receives any payment or partial payment of interest, if the payment arises from a payday loan agreement to receive interest that was entered into before that day.
-- src:19343 | Paragraph 347.1(2)(a.1) of Criminal Code
-- src:19344 | 615 Paragraph 347.1(2)(a.1) of the Criminal Code, as it reads on the day on which subsection 612(1) comes into force, does not apply to a person who
-- src:19345 | (a) entered into a payday loan agreement to receive interest before that day; or
-- src:19346 | (b) on or after that day, receives any payment or partial payment of interest, if the payment arises from a payday loan agreement to receive interest that was entered into before that day.
@ref 2023, c. 26, s. 615 (src:19343-19346)
GIVEN `the day on which subsection 612(1) of 2023, c. 26 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the person entered into the payday loan agreement to receive interest` IS A DATE
      `the day the person receives a payment or partial payment of interest` IS A DATE
      `the payment arises from a payday loan agreement to receive interest that was entered into before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2023 c 26 s 615 paragraph 347.1(2)(a.1), as it reads on that day, applies to the person` MEANS
    IF `limb (a): the person entered into a payday loan agreement to receive interest before that day` OR `limb (b): the person, on or after that day, receives a payment arising from an agreement entered into before that day`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply to a person who"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to a person who"
    WHERE
        `limb (a): the person entered into a payday loan agreement to receive interest before that day` MEANS
            `the day the person entered into the payday loan agreement to receive interest` LESS THAN `the day on which subsection 612(1) of 2023, c. 26 comes into force`
        `limb (b): the person, on or after that day, receives a payment arising from an agreement entered into before that day` MEANS
                `the day the person receives a payment or partial payment of interest` AT LEAST `the day on which subsection 612(1) of 2023, c. 26 comes into force`
            AND `the payment arises from a payday loan agreement to receive interest that was entered into before that day`

§ `2023, c. 30, s. 3 -- the amendments apply to ongoing proceedings`

-- 2023 c 30 s 3: a grant of application ("applies with respect to ... ongoing"): ongoing is JUST TRUE; any other matter is outside the grant's own wording (NOTHING).
-- src:19353 | Clarification
-- src:19354 | 3 For greater certainty, the amendments made by this Act also apply with respect to proceedings that are ongoing on the day on which this Act comes into force.
@ref 2023, c. 30, s. 3 (src:19353-19354)
GIVEN `the proceedings are ongoing on the day on which 2023, c. 30 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2023 c 30 s 3 the amendments made by 2023, c. 30 apply to the matter or proceeding` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are ongoing on the day on which 2023, c. 30 comes into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "also apply with respect to proceedings that are ongoing on the day on which this Act comes into force"


§ `2023, c. 32, s. 14.1 -- unlawfully manufactured firearms: proceedings already commenced`

-- 14.1 If proceedings in respect of an unlawfully manufactured firearm have been commenced before the day paragraph (e) of the definition prohibited firearm in 84(1) comes into force and have not been completed before that day,
-- then that paragraph (e) does not apply with respect to the firearm in relation to those proceedings. A flat negative under its own conditions; otherwise silent (NOTHING). Whether the firearm is a prohibited firearm is for s 84(1) (part ccc4).
-- src:19357 | Unlawfully manufactured firearms
-- src:19358 | 14.1 If proceedings in respect of an unlawfully manufactured firearm have been commenced under the Criminal Code before the day on which paragraph (e) of the definition prohibited firearm in subsection 84(1) of that Act, as enacted by subsection 1(1), comes into force and have not been completed before that day, then that paragraph (e) does not apply with respect to the firearm in relation to those proceedings.
@ref 2023, c. 32, s. 14.1 (src:19357-19358)
GIVEN `the day on which paragraph (e) of the definition prohibited firearm in subsection 84(1), as enacted by subsection 1(1) of 2023, c. 32, comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the day proceedings in respect of the unlawfully manufactured firearm were commenced under the Criminal Code` IS A DATE
      `the proceedings have been completed before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`2023 c 32 s 14.1 paragraph (e) of the definition prohibited firearm applies to the firearm in relation to those proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the day proceedings in respect of the unlawfully manufactured firearm were commenced under the Criminal Code` LESS THAN `the day on which paragraph (e) of the definition prohibited firearm in subsection 84(1), as enacted by subsection 1(1) of 2023, c. 32, comes into force`
       AND NOT `the proceedings have been completed before that day`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then that paragraph (e) does not apply with respect to the firearm in relation to those proceedings"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If proceedings in respect of an unlawfully manufactured firearm have been commenced under the Criminal Code before the day"
